  "text": "<p> [[762.1]] <b>215. ERHARD WEIGEL AN LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[762.2]] Jena, 28. Oktober (7. November) 1679 [212.]</b></p>\n<p> [[762.13]] [<i>K</i>] </p>\n<p> [[762.14]] Magnifice Vir! <Fn><i>Am Rande von Leibniz' Hand:</i> Weigelii <i>Vertical-Chaise</i></Fn> </p>\n<p> [[762.15]] Plus quam centum boum mactatione dignum existimo quod benevole mihi communicasti,\n[[762.16]] dispositionis progressionum arithmeticarum inventum, non tam quod inter infinitam unitatum\n[[762.17]] finitarum collectionem, et ipsam unitatem finitam, definitum medium reddat (infinitum enim\n[[762.18]] definiri contradictionem implicat, hinc ipsum medium vel quasi nempe <zl>1<ne>0<be> i. e. unum nihil,\n[[762.19]] indefinitum est) quam potius, quod facile conjiciam, immensum ex hoc artificio compendium\n[[762.20]] in Philosophiam demonstrativam redundaturum, et numerorum vim directam hinc nimium\n[[762.21]] quantum clare comparituram esse, praesertim accedente peculiaris Analyseos, quam meditaris,\n[[762.22]] usu. Quod utrunque bonum, ut urgeas, quantum possum oro. Ego interim numerorum vim\n[[762.23]] reflexam, qua Nullitatem nostram, hinc; inde, primi Motoris existentiam et indefessam operationem\n[[762.24]] eloquuntur, pro virili prosequar, utut hic loci locus inter philosophemata numeris\n[[762.25]] aegre relinquatur. </p>\n<p> [[762.26]] Quod in Cap. 2. Disp. meae prioris §. 1. n. 4. de puncto intimo, quod subtrahi tandem\n[[762.27]] postulatur, notasti, non eo trahendum est, quasi centrum magnitudinis intelligatur, cum sermo\n[[763.1]] sit de continua subtractione, vel si mavis, divisione seu remotione terminorum extremorum\n[[763.2]] circum circa rem, donec tandem ad punctum aliquod perveniatur, tanquam ad ultimum minimumque\n[[763.3]] conceptum, rei proxime positivum, quem ipsum etiam subtrahi postulo: quo facto\n[[763.4]] clare patet pure nihil remanere. </p>\n<p> [[763.5]] Spatium (sc. ubicativum, i.e. rerum juxta se mutuo simul existentium non-repugnantia\n[[763.6]] loco nihili, rerumque concepta) et Tempus in abstracto (tanquam Spatium quandicativum, i.e.\n[[763.7]] rerum omnium, ut unius copiae, secundum prius et posterius existentium i.e. repetitarum,\n[[763.8]] non-repugnantia loco nihili rerumque concepta) tanto magis analoga sunt inter se, quanto\n[[763.9]] praecisius utrumque dicit potentiam perceptibilis positionis, illud simultaneae hoc successivae,\n[[763.10]] quae non aliter in actum deducitur, quam si res ipsae finitae (plures simul, et quaelibet,\n[[763.11]] secundum prius et posterius) perceptibiliter ponuntur, et utrumque spatium occupant. </p>\n<p> [[763.12]] Tractatuum meorum nullus amplius ullo praestat exemplaris, praeter id quod editioni\n[[763.13]] secundae, si Bibliopola quispiam exorari tandem aliquam poterit, apud me servatur. </p>\n<p> [[763.14]] Ferrum repetitis vicibus candens redditum ipse vidi, nec ad effectum, ultra virgae ferreae\n[[763.15]] clavicularis conversionem cuivis ictui transversalem, ipsamque repetitionis aequabilitatem,\n[[763.16]] quicquam requiritur ab exercitato. </p>\n<p> [[763.17]] Caeterum, novum hoc quod descriptum hic legis, vehiculi genus quam vellem, ut Magnatibus\n[[763.18]] innotesceret. Nullus dubito, quin omnibus placiturum sit, imprimis Serenissimo Vestro,\n[[763.19]] qui si 100 imperiales arrhae loco (sub hypotheca meorum immobilium accipiendae) praenumerare;\n[[763.20]] ducentos insuper complendi pretii gratia, perfecto demum opere, mihi numerari, juberet,\n[[763.21]] vel menstruo spatio tantam itineri, praesertim longiori, commoditatem, cum ornamentis\n[[763.22]] principe dignis, obtinere posset. Id quod et Generoso Dⁿ^#'o a Wizendorff, et Tibi ni graveris,\n[[763.23]] commendatum relinquo. Vale faveque <+6> </p>\n<p> [[763.24]] Tuo <greek>^%(/olvw ^%(/ol^v</greek> E. Weigelio P.P. <+6>\n [[763.25]] Jenae d. 28. 8^#'b^#'r^#'i^#'s 1679. <+6> </p>\n<p> [[763.26]] <i>A Monsieur! Monsieur G.G. Leibnütz, mon Patron. à Hanover.</i> </p>\n<p> [[764.1]] [<i>LiK</i>] </p>\n[[764.2]] <petit> <e20><i>Die ersten drei folgenden, auf Bl. 4r^#'o stehenden Tabellen bzw. Berechnungen stellen von Leibniz gestrichene\n[[764.3]] Vorstufen oder Vorberechnungen für den nachfolgenden Beweis ab S. 990350.9 dar.</i> </petit> </p>\n<p> [[764.4]] <i>B</i> <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <tab/><zl>1<ne>4<be> <tab/><zl>1<ne>5<be> </p>\n<p> [[764.5]] <i>A</i> <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <tab/><zl>1<ne>10<be> <tab/><zl>1<ne>15<be> </p>\n<p> [[764.6]] <zl><i>A</i><ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <zl>1<ne>12<be> <tab/><zl>1<ne>20<be> <tab/><zl>1<ne>30<be> </p>\n<p> [[764.7]] + <i>B</i> ─ 1 <zl>1<ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>4<be> <zl>1<ne>5<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <tab/>\n [[764.8]] ^#1+ <tab/>^#1- </p>\n<p> [[764.9]] <i>B</i> <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>4<be> <zl>1<ne>5<be> [<i>bricht ab</i>] </p>\n<p> [[764.10]] Ostendendum est esse <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <zl>1<ne>10<be> <zl>1<ne>15<be> <zl>1<ne>21<be> etc. [<i>bricht ab</i>] </p>\n<p> [[764.11]] Ostendendum est </p>\n<p> [[764.12]] <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <tab/><zl>1<ne>10<be> <zl>1<ne>15<be> <zl>1<ne>21<be> etc. <tab/>esse aequal. 2 </p>\n<p> [[764.13]] Sint tres series </p>\n<p> [[764.14]] <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>5<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> etc. <tab/>quam vocemus <i>A</i> </p>\n<p> [[764.15]] <zl>1<ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>4<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <zl>1<ne>7<be> etc. <tab/>quam vocemus <i>B</i> </p>\n<p> [[764.16]] <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <zl>1<ne>15<be> <zl>1<ne>21<be> etc. <tab/>quam vocemus <i>C</i> </p>\n<p> [[764.17]] erit\n[[764.18]] <zl>1<ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <zl>1<ne>12<be> <zl>1<ne>30<be> <zl>1<ne>42<be> etc. <tab/>idem quod <zl>1<ne>2<be> <i>C</i> </p>\n<p> [[764.19]] et erit </p>\n<p> [[764.20]] <zl>1<ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>4<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <zl>1<ne>7<be> etc. </p>\n<p> [[764.21]] <tab/>idem quod <i>B</i> + <zl>1<ne>2<be> <i>C</i> </p>\n<p> [[765.1]] <zl>1<ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <zl>1<ne>12<be> <zl>1<ne>30<be> <zl>1<ne>42<be> etc.<tab/> </p>\n<p> [[765.2]] ^#1+ <tab/>^#1- </p>\n<p> [[765.3]] id est <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>5<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> etc. <tab/>idem quod [<i>bricht ab</i>] </p>\n<p> [[765.4]] Ostendendum est </p>\n[[765.5]] <petit> <e20><i>Die folgenden drei Reihen vor dem nächsten Absatz wurden von Leibniz gestrichen:</i> </petit>\n[[765.6]] <c06> <p><zl>1<ne>1<be> + <zl>1<ne>2<be> + <zl>1<ne>3<be> + <zl>1<ne>4<be> + <zl>1<ne>5<be> + <zl>1<ne>6<be> + <zl>1<ne>7<be> + <zl>1<ne>8<be> + <zl>1<ne>9<be> + <zl>1<ne>10<be> + <zl>1<ne>11<be> </p>\n<p> [[765.7]] <zl>1<ne>2<be> + <zl>1<ne>6<be> + <zl>1<ne>12<be> + <zl>1<ne>20<be> + <zl>1<ne>30<be> + <zl>1<ne>42<be> + <zl>1<ne>56<be> + <zl>1<ne>72<be> + <zl>1<ne>90<be> + <zl>1<ne>110<be> ^&.sc <Leibniz special character> <zl>1<ne>1<be> + <zl>1<ne>11<be> ^&.sc <Leibniz special character> <zl>10<ne>11<be> </p>\n<p> [[765.8]] <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <zl>1<ne>10<be> <zl>1<ne>15<be> <zl>1<ne>21<be> <zl>1<ne>28<be> <zl>1<ne>36<be> <zl>1<ne>45<be> <zl>1<ne>55<be> </p>\n<p> [[766.1]] Eadem methodus qua summam hujus seriei infinitae inveni, servit etiam ad summam finiti\n[[766.2]] numeri terminorum hujus seriei inveniendam, exempli causa quaeritur summa horum 10 terminorum\n[[766.3]] <zl>1<ne>1<be> + <zl>1<ne>3<be> + <zl>1<ne>6<be> + <zl>1<ne>10<be> + <zl>1<ne>15<be> + <zl>1<ne>21<be> + <zl>1<ne>28<be> + <zl>1<ne>36<be> + <zl>1<ne>45<be> + <zl>1<ne>55<be> . <+4> Regula eam compendio\n[[766.4]] inveniendi haec est sane mirabilis: numerus fractionum 10 duplicatus, nempe 20 dividatur per\n[[766.5]] 11 numerum nempe fractionum unitate auctum. </p>\n",
  "number": "215.",
  "title": "ERHARD WEIGEL AN LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "Jena, 28. Oktober (7. November) 1679 [212.]"
};
